value":1.359,"value_relation":"=","std":0.07,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.4c00406","year":2024,"record_id":"MLDB-002719","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The log Po/w of the prepared complexes (Ru2L1, Ir2L1, Re2L1, Ru2L2, Ir2L2, and Re2L2) were determined by dint of shake flask method using the previously published procedure. A known amount of each complex was suspended in water (pre-saturated with n-octanol) and shaken for 48 h on an orbital shaker. To permit phase separation, the solution was centrifuged for 10 min at 3000 rpm. To get the partition coefficient, different ratios (1:2, 1:1, and 2:1) of the saturated solutions were shaken with pre-saturated n-octanol for 20 min on an orbital shaker and followed the same procedure. Aliquots of the aqueous and octanol layers were pipetted out separately and the absorbance was measured with a UV-Vis spectrophotometer using proper dilution. The partition coefficient (log Po/w) values were obtained from the ratio of absorbance value."}]}